// First, we check tools that modify the order in a sequence

_retro A3 B3 C3 1/4 D3

[Propagate in polymetric structure] 
_retro {a b {c d, C4 D4}} 1/4

_retro {a b {3, c d, C4 D4}}

[Cascading _retro] 
_retro {a b _retro {c d _retro {A4 B4}}}

[Equivalent, yet less intuitive] 
_retro a b _retro c d _retro A4 B4

[Will always produce the same order because seed = 1] 
_rndseq a b c d

[Here, the order will change because to the _randomize command] 
_randomize _rndseq a b c d

[No effect] 
_randomize a b c d

[_randomize is misplaced, as it will be contained in the sequence] 
_rndseq _randomize a b c d

[The second part is not randomised] 
_rndseq a b c d _ordseq A5 B5 C5

[Same example with _retro] 
_retro a b c d _ordseq A5 B5 C5

